  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nHow many shrimp can Emily peel and saute in ten minutes? Emily can peel 7 shrimp per minute. Emily has 100 unpeeled shrimp available. Emily works continuously for the entire ten-minute period.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "LOSSY SELF-SUMMARY; VERIFY AGAINST NEW INPUTS\nVISIBLE PREFIX THROUGH TURN 6; LOSSY EXTRACT:\n- {\"content\":\"Actually, that was wrong. Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 10 minutes.\",\"role\":\"user\"}\n- {\"content\":\"Emily can peel:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n6 \\\\times 10=60\\n\\\\]\\n\\nAfter discarding 5 damaged shrimp, she has:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n60-5=55\\n\\\\]\\n\\nusable shrimp. Since she can sauté 30 shrimp in 10 minutes, she can sauté:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{30}\\n\\\\]\\n\\nshri...\n- {\"content\":\"Here's another detail: Emily peels and sautes each shrimp sequentially rather than simultaneously.\",\"role\":\"user\"}\n- {\"content\":\"Emily’s rates are:\\n\\n- Peeling: \\\\(6\\\\) shrimp/minute, so each takes \\\\(\\\\frac{1}{6}\\\\) minute.\\n- Sautéing: \\\\(30\\\\) shrimp in \\\\(10\\\\) minutes \\\\(=3\\\\) shrimp/minute, so each takes \\\\(\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\) minute.\\n\\nSince sh...",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Got it. But now I only need to know about: How long will it take Emily to peel and cook the shrimp? By the way, Emily needs to peel and cook 90 shrimp.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily’s peeling rate is \\(7\\) shrimp per minute, so peeling \\(90\\) shrimp takes\n\n\\[\n\\frac{90}{7}\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\n\nHer sautéing rate is \\(30\\) shrimp per \\(10\\) minutes, or \\(3\\) shrimp per minute. Thus, cooking \\(90\\) shrimp takes\n\n\\[\n\\frac{90}{3}=30\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\n\nSince she peels and cooks sequentially, the total time is\n\n\\[\n\\frac{90}{7}+30\n=\\frac{300}{7}\n=42\\frac{6}{7}\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, it will take approximately\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{42\\text{ minutes }51\\text{ seconds}}.\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
